          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. A mixture containing potatoes, salt and sawdust has been given to you. Outline a stepwise procedure for separating each component from this mixture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.148,
            0.883,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. Read the following story titled ‘Intelligent Leela’ and tick the most appropriate options. Provide a suitable title of your choice for the paragraph."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.214,
            0.884,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Leela was working in the farm with her father when she realised that they left their drinking water at home. Before her father felt "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "thirsty/hungry",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", she went to the nearby pond to fetch some "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "water/grains",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". After obtaining some water in the container, she noticed that the water was muddy and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "fit/unfit",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for drinking. To purify the water, she kept it for some time and then she "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "filtered/ churned",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the muddy water using a piece of "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "paper/muslin cloth",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Leela, then, "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "cooled/boiled",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the water for about 10 minutes in a covered pan. After "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "cooling/boiling",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", she "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "filtered/churned",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " it again and made it "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "fit/unfit",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for drinking. She served this water to her father while having food, who blessed her and appreciated her efforts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.389,
            0.472,
            0.638,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Learning further"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.523,
            0.883,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fun with parents:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We are proud of our Indian heritage. Under supervision of your elders, try to prepare some herbal remedies using various parts of plants. For example—tulsi kadha. Which methods of separation will you use while preparing herbal kadha?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.625,
            0.884,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Stage play:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Imagine you and your friend are Malli and Valli. Write dialogues of a play presenting their entire ‘Bharat ki Yatra’, highlighting the different methods of separation of substances that they observed. Enact the play in your school assembly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.285,
            0.725,
            0.884,
            0.824
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Group activity:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Observe and list separation methods you employed and noticed in your surroundings throughout a week. Explain the reasons behind using these methods and compile the ones you utilised or observed the most. Compare your observations with your group members."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.828,
            0.884,
            0.923
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Be a stalwart of your community:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Interview a ragpicker(s) and prepare a case study about the method(s) of separation he/she uses in his/her daily life. Encourage children of your community below the age of 14 to join a neighbourhood school."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
